Subject: [PATCH 7/7] zuma: keep the built images in target-files

target-files made its system, system_ext, product, vendor, vendor_dlkm
and system_dlkm images again from their folders, with
ro.build.date.utc as every file's time, while the images the build
flashes keep each file's time in out/. The OTA package is made
from target-files' images and the fastboot zip from the build's, so
an incremental OTA, which checks every source block it reads, would
refuse phones installed from the fastboot zip.

COPY_IMAGES_FOR_TARGET_FILES_ZIP has target-files take the built
images (and makes their file times fixed). It takes only images whose
file system type is set to ext4 or erofs, and zuma already sets ext4
for all six, so that's the only line needed.

This covers the six dynamic partitions, the ones an incremental patches
block by block. target-files still makes its own init_boot,
vendor_boot, vendor_kernel_boot, dtbo and vbmeta (signed with other AVB
salts), so an incremental from it has to write those whole
(ota_from_target_files --full_ota_partitions). Same as cheetah's
gs201 change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 BoardConfig-common.mk | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/BoardConfig-common.mk b/BoardConfig-common.mk
index ac2d574d..278bee22 100644
--- a/BoardConfig-common.mk
+++ b/BoardConfig-common.mk
@@ -146,6 +146,12 @@ BOARD_USERDATAIMAGE_PARTITION_SIZE := 11796480000
 PRODUCT_FS_COMPRESSION := 1
 BOARD_FLASH_BLOCK_SIZE := 4096
 
+# ExpressiveOS: target-files takes the images the build made instead of making them
+# again, so they're the very images the fastboot zip flashes, and an incremental OTA
+# from a build applies on phones installed from its fastboot zip too. It takes only
+# images whose file system type is set to ext4 or erofs, as each one's is below.
+COPY_IMAGES_FOR_TARGET_FILES_ZIP := true
+
 # system.img
 BOARD_SYSTEMIMAGE_FILE_SYSTEM_TYPE := ext4
 
